description:
Write the broad phase of lesson 3.05:

```cpp
struct Rectangle { float x, y, width, height; };

class SpatialGrid
{
public:
    SpatialGrid(float cellSize, int cols, int rows);
    void clear();
    void insert(int id, Rectangle r);
    std::vector<int> query(Rectangle area) const;                     // ids of objects overlapping area, sorted, each once
    std::vector<std::pair<int, int>> overlappingPairs() const;        // (a, b) with a < b, sorted, each once
    int testsMade() const;                                            // narrow-phase tests in the last overlappingPairs
};
```

- An object goes into every cell its rectangle touches. Cell coordinates are `floor(x / cellSize)`, clamped to the grid; the far edge uses the rectangle's right and bottom (`x + width`, `y + height`).
- `query` looks only in the cells the area covers, and returns objects whose rectangles really overlap the area (touching does not count).
- `overlappingPairs` tests each pair of objects that share a cell, once only, and keeps those whose rectangles really overlap. `testsMade` counts how many distinct pairs were tested.

